hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Rabi’ bin Sulayman says that I heard Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding the hadith of the Prophet (peace be upon him): “Whoever does not recite the Qur’an with a pleasant voice is not from among us,” say: (that the meaning of this hadith is) that we should recite it with a sorrowful voice and with measured recitation."
"1202","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Whoever does not recite the Qur’an with a pleasant voice is not from among us.”"
"1203","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not honor the elder, does not show mercy to the younger, does not enjoin good, and does not forbid evil, is not from among us."
"1204","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with her), who was the wife of Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) and the half-sister of Uthman bin Affan, that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That person is not a liar who reconciles between two people, so (for this purpose) he says a good word or conveys a good word."
"1205","Sayyida Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There is no concession for lying except in three things."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""I do not count these (three) as liars: the person who reconciles between people and says something (untrue) for the sake of reconciliation, and the person who says something (untrue) in war, and the person who says something (untrue) to his wife, and the wife who says something (untrue) to her husband."
"1206","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That person is not a liar who reconciles between people, so (for this purpose) he says a good word or conveys a good word."
"1207","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abundance of possessions is not wealth; true wealth is the richness of the heart (contentment)."
"1208","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abundance of possessions is not wealth; rather, true wealth is the richness of the heart (contentment)."
"1209","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O people! Abundance of possessions is not wealth; true wealth is the richness of the heart. Then indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will give every servant his complete sustenance that He has written for him, so seek sustenance in a good manner, take what is lawful and leave what is unlawful."
"1210","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abundance of possessions is not wealth, rather (true) wealth is the richness of the heart (contentment)."" Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) as a marfu' (attributed to the Prophet) narration."
"1211","This hadith is also narrated in the same way from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain of transmission."
"1212","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who overpowers others in wrestling is not strong and brave; rather, the strong and brave one is he who controls himself when he is angry."" (Imam) Malik has narrated this hadith through five narrators as follows: Qanabi said «عن مالك» (from Malik); Ibn Yusuf said «انبانا مالك» (Malik informed us); Ibn Safir said «حدثني مالك» (Malik narrated to me); Ibn Bukair said «ثنا مالك» (Malik narrated to us); and Ibn Wahb said «اخبرني مالك» (Malik informed me). Muslim bin Hajjaj has also narrated it in a similar manner from Yahya bin Sa'id and Abdullah bin Hammad with his chain, both of whom said: «قرأت على مالك» (I recited to Malik)."
"1213","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing more noble in the sight of Allah than supplication (du'a)."
"1214","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing more noble in the sight of Allah than supplication (du'a)."
"1215","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing is swifter than the punishment for rebellion and defiance."
"1216","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Nothing is better than a believer among a thousand things like itself."
"1217","Mutarrif bin Abdullah narrates from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and I heard him reciting: ﴿أَلْهَاكُمُ التَّكَاثُرُ﴾ (At-Takathur: 1) ""The mutual rivalry for piling up (worldly things) diverts you."" (Then) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth, whereas from your wealth only that is yours which you have consumed and finished, or worn and worn out, or given in charity and sent ahead."
"1218","Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “The best remembrance is the hidden remembrance, and the best provision is that which suffices.”"
"1219","This narration is also reported through another chain from Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman."
"1220","Muhammad bin Abdur Rahman bin Labeebah says that Umar bin Sa’d said to his father: You are among the people of Badr and among those whom Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) chose for the Shura. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The best provision is that which suffices, and the best remembrance is the hidden remembrance."
"1221","Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best visit to the sick is that which is done in the most discreet manner."" This hadith is concise."
"1222","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best gatherings are those which are spacious.”"
"1223","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Amrah Ansari reports that Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) was informed of a funeral in his tribe. He was delayed until the people had already sat in their places. Then he came, and when the people saw him coming, they began to make room for him. Some of them stood up so that he could sit in their place. He then said: Listen! Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The best gatherings are those which are spacious."" Then he moved aside and sat in an open space."
"1224","Abdullah bin Shaqiq reports that it was said to Sayyiduna Mihjan Deeli (may Allah be pleased with him): Why do you not pray as much as so-and-so prays? He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The best part of your religion is that which is easiest."
"1225","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your religion is that which is the easiest."" Al-Tabarani said: Only Salam narrated it from Qatadah, and Isma'il ibn Yazid is unique in narrating it."
"1226","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best marriage is that which is the easiest."
"1227","Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best charity is that after which a person remains self-sufficient, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin (charity and kindness) with those whom you support."
"1228","Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin (charity and alms) with those whom you support, and the best charity is that after which a person remains self-sufficient. And whoever seeks to be saved, Allah will save him, and whoever seeks to be independent, Allah will make him independent."
"1229","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and each of you should begin (charity and alms) with those whom he supports, and the best charity is that after which a person remains self-sufficient. Whoever seeks to be saved, Allah will save him, and whoever seeks to be independent, Allah will make him independent."
"1230","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"1231","This hadith is also narrated in the same manner from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) through another chain of transmission."
"1232","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The best charity is that which is given when a person is still wealthy after giving it, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and start (charity) with those whom you support."
"1233","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard this sermon from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in Tabuk. I heard him say in a long sermon: ""The best deed is that which brings benefit, and the best guidance is that which is followed, and the best thing placed in the heart is certainty."
"1234","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among people is the one who is most beneficial to (other) people."" This hadith is concise."
"1235","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best companion in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best neighbor in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."
"1236","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Aktham bin Abi Al-Junoon: ""O Aktham! The best companions for a journey are four, and the best vanguard is of four hundred, and the best army is of four thousand."
"1237","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best companions are four, and the best group of fighters is four hundred, and the best army is four thousand, and an army of twelve thousand can never be defeated merely due to lack of numbers."
"1238","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Aktham bin Abi al-Junoon: ""O Aktham! The best number of companions for a journey is four, and the best vanguard is of forty, and the best fighting group is of four hundred, and the best army is of four thousand. And an army of twelve thousand cannot be defeated merely due to lack of numbers. O Aktham! If you perform jihad along with people other than your own tribe, your character will improve and you will become honorable in the eyes of your companions."
"1239","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best companions are four, and the best group of fighters is four hundred, and the best army is four thousand, and an army of twelve thousand can never be defeated merely due to small numbers as long as they remain patient and speak the truth."
"1240","Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). One narrator said: (that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said:) ""The best among you."" And another narrator said: (that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said:) ""The best among you is the one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it (to others)."
"1241","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it (to others)."
"1242","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best among you is the one who learns the Qur’an and teaches it (to others).”"
"1243","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one who is best to his family."
"1244","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one who is best to his family, and I am the best among you to my family."
"1245","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Kabsha (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one who is best to his family."
"1246","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one from whom good is expected and people are safe from his evil, and the worst among you is the one from whom good is not expected and people are not safe from his evil."
"1247","This hadith is also narrated from Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad through another chain that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Shall I not inform you about your good and bad people?"" So a man said: Why not. Then the Prophet said . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"1248","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not inform you about your good and bad people? Your good people are those from whose evil others are safe and from whom good is expected, and your bad people are those from whom good is not expected and from whose evil others are not safe."
"1249","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your homes is the one in which an orphan is honored."
"1250","Suwaid bin Hubairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best wealth is a path lined with fruitful date palms or a mare that bears many offspring."
"1251","Suwaid bin Hubairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best wealth of a person is a she-goat that bears many offspring or a path lined with fruitful date-palms."" In Mu'jam Ibn al-A'rabi, it is narrated in the same way from Muslim bin Nadhir, and the scholars of hadith have also narrated it similarly. However, in Abu Ubaid's ""Gharib al-Hadith,"" it is from Muslim bin Badeel. And Abu Muhammad has mentioned Suwaid bin Hubairah in «مسند الصحابة من الصحابة» (in it) with this very hadith."
"1252","Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The best mosques for women are the innermost parts of their houses."
"1253","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of your clothes are the white ones, so clothe your living in them and shroud your dead in them. And indeed, the best of your kohl is antimony (ithmid), for it sharpens the eyesight and causes the eyelashes to grow."
"1254","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best kohl among you is antimony, which sharpens the eyesight and grows the eyelashes. And the best clothes among you are white, so clothe your living in them and shroud your dead in them as well."
"1255","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of your young men are those who resemble your elders, and the worst of your elders are those who resemble your young men."
"1256","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best rows among the men are their first rows, and the worst are their last rows; and the best rows among the women are their last rows, and the worst are their first rows.”"
"1257","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"1258","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The best rows among the men's rows in prayer are the front rows, and the worst are the last rows. And the best rows among the women's rows are the last rows, and the worst are the front rows."
"1259","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best rows among the men are their first rows, and the worst are their last rows; and the best rows among the women are their last rows, and the worst are their first rows.”"
"1260","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"1261","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “That which is little but sufficient is better than that which is abundant but distracts.”"
"1262","This narration is also reported through another chain from Muhammad bin Awf with his chain in the same manner."
"1263","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Turn to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. That which is little but sufficient is better than that which is abundant but distracts. O people! Indeed, there are two paths: one is the path of good and the other is the path of evil. So whoever prefers the path of evil over the path of good has surely perished. O people! Protect yourselves from the Fire, even if it be with a piece of a date."
"1264","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world is a provision, and the best provision of it is a righteous woman."
"1265","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world is a provision, and the best provision of the world is a righteous woman."" Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world is a provision, and the best provision of the world is a righteous woman."
"1266","Ibn Shaniyyah says that I saw Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) sitting alone in the mosque, wrapped in a woolen cloak with a border. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Solitude is better than a bad companion, and a good companion is better than solitude. Dictating a good word is better than silence, and silence is better than dictating a bad word."
"1267","This narration is also reported through another chain from Bishm bin Jameel with his chain in the same manner."
"1268","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “To complete a (first) good deed is better than to begin (another) good deed.”"
"1269","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “To complete a (first) good deed is better than to begin (another) good deed.”"
"1270","Hasan al-Basri says that it has reached us that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A small deed according to the Sunnah is better than a lot of deeds according to innovation."
"1271","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you are those who are afflicted with trials and who repent abundantly."
"1272","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among you are those who are best in fulfilling (their obligations)."
"1273","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) . . . and he narrated this hadith and in it he said: ""Indeed, the best among you is the one who is best in repayment."
"1274","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best among the believers are those who are content, and the worst among them are those who are greedy."
"1275","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""The best among the believers are those who are content, and the worst among them are those who are greedy."
"1276","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people of my Ummah are its scholars, and the best of its scholars are those who are forbearing. Listen! Indeed, before Allah forgives one sin of a hard-hearted ignorant person, He forgives forty sins of a compassionate scholar. And indeed, the compassionate scholar will come on the Day of Resurrection in such a state that his light will be shining. He will walk in that (light) as a shining star."" Imam Hakim (may Allah have mercy on him) said: (Its chain) the narrator Ibn Muslima is Muhammad bin Muslima Madini, and he is not Muhammad bin Muslima Qanabi."
"1277","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people of my Ummah are those quick-tempered ones who, when they become angry, (soon) swallow it."
"1278","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best people of my Ummah are those quick-tempered ones who, when they become angry, (soon) swallow it."
"1279","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best charity is that of the tongue.” It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the charity of the tongue? He said: “Interceding through which you free a captive, save someone from being killed, do good and show kindness to your brother, and remove a calamity from him.”"
"1280","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best charity is to mend mutual relationships."
"1281","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best charity is to reconcile relationships among people."
"1282","Sayyida Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The best charity is that which is given to a relative who harbors enmity and hatred."
"1283","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best act of worship is to await prosperity."" No one except Baqiyyah has narrated it with a connected chain from Imam Malik."
"1284","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The most virtuous act of worship of my Ummah is the recitation of the Qur’an.”"
"1285","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best virtue is to honor one's companions."
"1286","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best jihad is to speak a word of truth before a tyrannical ruler.”"
"1287","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The best jihad is to speak a word of truth and justice before a tyrannical ruler or a tyrannical leader.”"
"1288","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man said near the first Jamrah: O Messenger of Allah! Which jihad is the best? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned away from him, then he asked: ""Where is that questioner?"" The narrator says that the man said: O Messenger of Allah! I am here. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best jihad is that of a person who speaks a word of truth before a tyrant ruler."
"1289","Sahl bin Mu’adh narrates from his father, who narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: “The best deed is that you maintain ties with the one who severs relations with you, give to the one who deprives you, and forgive the one who wrongs you.”"
"1290","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best act of worship is understanding of the religion, and the virtue over religion is modesty."
"1291","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith: ""The believer with the most complete faith is the one who has the best character."
"1292","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The virtue of knowledge is greater than worship."
"1293","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no deed better than feeding a hungry person."
"1294","Zamrah bin Habib bin Suhaib reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is nothing by which a servant draws nearer to Allah than a hidden prostration."
"1295","Ayub bin Musa narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No father has given his children any gift better than good manners."
"1296","Ayub bin Musa narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No father has given his children any gift better than good manners."
"1297","Ayub bin Musa al-Qurashi narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""No father has given his children any gift better than good manners."
"1298","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was weeping, so he said: ""Mu'adh! Why are you weeping?"" He replied: ""Because of the hadith which I heard from the one in this grave, meaning the Prophet (peace be upon him), that: 'Indeed, even a small amount of showing off is shirk, and the unknown pious people are Allah's beloved servants. When they are absent from a gathering, they are not sought after, and when they are present, they are not recognized. These people are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge.'"
"1299","Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty loves the servant who adopts gentleness when buying, selling, paying, and demanding."
"1300","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “May Allah have mercy on the servant who adopts gentleness when giving and also maintains gentleness when demanding.” Tabarani said: No one has narrated this from Muhammad bin Munkadir except Abu Ghassan."
"1301","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The most beloved places to Allah Almighty are the mosques."
"1302","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the most beloved deeds to Allah Almighty are those which are done consistently, even if they are few.”"
"1303","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The most beloved deeds to Allah are those that are done consistently, even if they are few."
"1304","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Adhere to those deeds which you are able to do, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not tire, but you tire. And indeed, the most beloved deeds to Allah are those which are done consistently, even if they are few.”"
"1305","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, the most beloved of people to Allah and the closest to Him in assembly will be the just ruler."
"1306","Ahmad bin Ibrahim Mosuli says that we were in Shamasiya with Caliph Mamun. On one side of him was Yahya bin Aktham. The Caliph looked towards the people and said to Yahya: Do you not see, Yusuf bin Atiyyah narrated to me from Thabit, who narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All creation is Allah's dependents (under His care); among them, the most beloved to Him is the one who is most beneficial to His dependents."
"1307","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved prayer to Allah from among a woman's prayers is the one she performs in the darkest part of her house."
"1308","Hasan reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no gulp more beloved to Allah than the gulp of anger which a servant swallows (for the sake of Allah's pleasure), or the gulp of patience at the time of calamity. And there is no drop more beloved to Allah than the tear that falls out of fear of Allah, or the drop of blood shed in the way of Allah."
"1309","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the Qur'an will be an excellent intercessor for its companion (the one who recites it)."
"1310","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Recite the Qur'an, for it will be an excellent intercessor for its companion on the Day of Resurrection."
"1311","Zaid bin Aslam narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that: ""How excellent a gift it is to say a word from among the words of wisdom, which a Muslim hears, then adopts it, and (considering it a trust) conveys it to his Muslim brother."
"1312","Musa bin Ja'far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Husayn bin Ali bin Abi Talib narrates that my father (Ja'far) narrated to me from his forefathers that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Date palms are indeed excellent wealth, for they remain firm in mud and provide food during drought."
"1313","This narration is also reported through another chain from Hasan bin Abdur Rahman bin Khallad with his chain in the same manner."
"1314","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the date palm tree, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It remains firm in the mud."" The complete hadith was narrated."
"1315","Sayyiduna Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “How excellent is lawful wealth for a righteous man.” This hadith is concise."
"1316","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the best gift or the best present from wise speech is that word which a person hears, then learns it and teaches it to his brother (this thing is) better for him than a year’s worship.”"
"1317","Muhammad bin Munkadir reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Wealth is an excellent helper for the fear of Allah, the Exalted."
"1318","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: ""There is no bad omen, but a good omen is indeed a good thing."
"1319","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent condiment vinegar is."
"1320","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent condiment vinegar is! And it is sufficient evil for a person that he dislikes whatever is brought near to him."
"1321","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What an excellent condiment vinegar is, and it is sufficient evil for a person that he dislikes whatever is brought near to him."
"1322","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best place of worship for a Muslim is his home."
"1323","Ismail bin Hasan Bukhari narrated with the chain of the sermon, which is reported by Zaid bin Khalid al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, whose mention has passed earlier. He mentioned that sermon, and in it was also: ""The truest word is the Book of Allah, the strongest handhold is the word of Taqwa, the best way is the way of the Prophets, and the most honorable and noble death is the death of a martyr."
"1324","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that we went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. . . . . . . And he mentioned it briefly."
"1325","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say while delivering the sermon: “There are two fundamental things: the way and the speech. So the truest statement is the Book of Allah, and the best way is the way of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). The worst matters are the newly invented things (in religion), and every innovation is misguidance. Do not desire a long life among you, nor let hope make you heedless. Everything that is coming is near. Wretched is the one who is declared wretched in his mother’s womb, and fortunate is the one who takes a lesson from others (bad outcomes). Beware! Indeed, fighting a believer is disbelief, and abusing him is wickedness. It is not lawful for any Muslim to sever relations with another Muslim for more than three days. The worst narrations are false narrations. It is not permissible to lie, neither seriously nor in jest. And a man should not make a promise to his son that he cannot fulfill (later). Indeed, truth leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise, and indeed, falsehood leads to sin, and sin leads to Hell.”"
"1326","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best fragrance is musk."
"1327","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The chief of your condiments is salt."
"1328","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication that is accepted the quickest is the supplication of an absent person for another absent person."
"1329","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The prayer that is accepted the quickest is the prayer of an absent person for another absent person."
"1330","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer that is accepted the quickest is the prayer of an absent person for another absent person."
"1331","Sayyiduna Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) says that after hearing this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I do not trust anyone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""Indeed, the heart of the son of Adam changes more quickly than a pot when it is boiling intensely."
"1332","Sayyiduna Miqdad bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I do not trust anyone. I heard him say... and he narrated this hadith."
"1333","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How excellent are those who use the toothstick from among my Ummah."
"1334","Abu Qilabah says that Sayyiduna Abu Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) asked Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him), or Abu Mas’ud asked Abu Abdullah, “What have you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say about «زعموا» ?” He said: I heard him (peace and blessings be upon him) say about it: “They claim that it is a very bad mount for a man.”"
"1335","Abu Qilabah says that Abu Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zam'u is a very bad mount for a man."" Qadi Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Salamah bin Ja'far Quda'i said: In my opinion, the Abu Abdullah mentioned in this hadith refers to Hudhayfah bin Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him), because he used to stay in Kufa with Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), they would sit together and ask each other questions. And Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) had the kunyah Abu Abdullah."
"1336","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was asked: What did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say about “za‘amū”? He said: “It is a very bad mount for a man.”"
"1337","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and then he narrated a long hadith in which he mentioned a lengthy sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), in which it was said: ""The worst matters are the newly introduced affairs (in religion), and the worst blind person is the one who is blind of heart. The worst excuse is the one made at the time of death, and the worst shame is the shame on the Day of Resurrection. The worst food is the consumption of an orphan's wealth, and the worst earning is the earning from adultery."
"1338","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst thing in a man is wailing miserliness or heart-extracting cowardice."
"1339","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) . . . . and he mentioned this hadith and (your) sermon, and in it was also: ""Misguidance after guidance is the greatest blindness, and a lying tongue is the greatest error."
"1340","Sayyiduna Miqdam bin Ma’dikarib رضي الله عنه narrates from the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم that he صلى الله عليه وسلم said: “The son of Adam has not filled any vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the son of Adam to eat a few morsels that keep his back straight, and if he must eat more, then a third (of his stomach) should be for food, a third for drink, and a third for breathing.”"
"1341","Sayyiduna Miqdam bin Ma’dikarib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say... and he narrated this hadith."
"1342","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my Ahl al-Bayt is like the Ark of Noah; whoever boarded it was saved, and whoever remained behind was drowned."
"1343","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my Ahl al-Bayt is like the Ark of Noah; whoever boarded it was saved, and whoever remained behind was drowned. And whoever fought against us in the last era, it is as if he fought alongside the Dajjal (against us)."
"1344","This narration is also reported through another chain from Muslim bin Ibrahim with his chain in the same manner."
"1345","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my Ahl al-Bayt is like the Ark of Noah; whoever boarded it was saved, and whoever remained behind was drowned."
"1346","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my companions is like that of stars; whoever follows any of their actions will be guided."
"1347","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the example of my Companions in my Ummah is like that of salt in food; food becomes delicious only with salt."
"1348","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my Companions in my Ummah is like that of salt in food; indeed, food becomes delicious only with salt."
"1349","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The example of my Ummah is like that of rain; it is not known whether there is goodness in its beginning or in its end."
"1350","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"1351","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"1352","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of my Ummah is like that of rain; it is not known whether there is goodness in its beginning or in its end."
"1353","Sayyiduna Abu Razin Uqayli (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a believer is like that of a honeybee, which eats only that which is pure and produces only that which is pure."
"1354","Sayyiduna Abu Dharrin ‘Aqeeli, may Allah be pleased with him, reports that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The example of a believer is like that of a honeybee, which eats only what is pure and produces only what is pure.”"
"1355","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""The example of a believer and his faith is like that of a horse tied to its stake, which jumps and leaps but then returns to its stake."
"1356","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The example of a believer and his faith is like that of a horse tied to its stake, which jumps and leaps (away) but then returns to its stake. Indeed, the believer also jumps and leaps (i.e., forgets), but then returns to faith.”"
"1357","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The example of a strong believer is like that of a date palm tree, and the example of a weak believer is like that of a young plant."
"1358","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a strong believer is like that of a date palm tree, and the example of a weak believer is like that of a young plant in a field."
"1359","Mujahid says that I accompanied Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) between Makkah and Madinah (on the way), and he did not narrate to me any hadith from the Prophet (peace be upon him) except this single hadith, and in it was: ""The example of the believer."" This hadith is narrated in Hasan bin Abdur Rahman bin Khallad Ramahurmuzi's book ""Kitab al-Amthal"" with a chain from Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Musa from Sulaiman bin Ayyub, and in it is: ""(The example of the strong believer) is like a date palm, and (the example of the weak believer) is like a young plant of a crop."
"1360","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The example of a believer is like that of a stalk (of grain) which the wind moves; sometimes it stands upright and sometimes it falls down. And the example of a disbeliever is like that of a pine tree which always stands straight until it is uprooted all at once."
"1361","It is narrated through another chain that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The example of a believer is like a young plant of a crop, which the wind moves; sometimes it makes it stand upright and sometimes it bends it down."" And he narrated the rest of the hadith as well."
"1362","It is narrated with another chain that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The example of a believer is like that of a stalk, which the wind moves; sometimes it falls down and sometimes it stands upright. And the example of a disbeliever is like that of a pine tree; indeed, the pine always stands upright until (at once) it is uprooted."
"1363","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The example of a believer is like that of a stalk of grain which the wind moves; sometimes it bends down and sometimes it stands upright. And the example of a disbeliever is like that of a pine or cedar tree (a hard type of tree from which sticks and the like are made) which always stands straight until (suddenly, all at once) it is uprooted.”"
"1364","Sayyiduna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a believer is like a tender plant of a crop which the winds keep bending this way and that, and the example of a hypocrite is like a pine tree which stands straight on the ground until it is uprooted all at once."" Abu Amr said: «ارزہ» is with a fatha on the ra and it is from «ارزن» . Abu Ubaid said: The pronunciation of «ارزہ» is like «فاعلہ» . Abu Ubaid also said that «ارزہ» is with a sukoon on the ra and it is the tree of pine. The meaning of «المجدیہ» is: straight. The meaning of «انجعاف» is: to be uprooted. And it is also said that the word «انجعاف» is with a kha instead of a jeem, «انخعاف» ."
"1365","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b رضي الله عنه narrates from the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم that he صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""The example of a believer is like a young plant of a crop which the winds keep turning this way and that; sometimes it is bent down and sometimes it is made straight. And the example of a disbeliever is like a pine tree which stands straight, its root is not separated (from the ground) until it is uprooted all at once."
"1366","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The example of the believers in their mutual love, mercy, and compassion is like that of a body; when any part of it is afflicted, the whole body remains awake and suffers from fever.”"
"1367","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, in their mutual love, mercy, and compassion, the example of the believers is like that of a single body; when any part of it suffers, the whole body responds with sleeplessness and fever.”"
"1368","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surely, in maintaining mutual relations, showing mercy and kindness among themselves, and in that which Allah has ordained between them, the example of the Muslims is like that of a body; when any part of it is afflicted with pain, the whole body becomes restless and suffers from sleeplessness and fever."
"1369","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the heart is like a feather lying on the ground, which the winds keep turning over and over."
"1370","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the Qur'an is like that of a camel whose leg is tied; if its owner keeps it tied, he will keep hold of it, and if he lets it go, it will run away."
"1371","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a hypocrite is like a goat wandering confusedly between two flocks."
"1372","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The example of a hypocrite is like a goat wandering confusedly between two herds, not knowing which of the two to follow."
"1373","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated it as marfu‘: “The example of a hypocrite is like a goat wandering confusedly between two herds.”"
"1374","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a hypocrite is like a goat wandering between two herds, sometimes running towards one herd (in search of a male goat for mating) and sometimes towards the other herd; it does not know which of the two it should follow."
"1375","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The example of a woman is like a crooked rib; if you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you benefit from her, then benefit from her while she is in this crooked state."
"1376","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""A woman is like a crooked rib; if you try to straighten her, you will break her, and if you benefit from her, you will benefit from her while she is crooked."
"1377","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a marfu‘ (attributed to the Prophet) narration that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The example of a good companion is like that of a perfume seller; even if he does not give you any perfume as a gift, its fragrance will surely reach you. And the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith who blows the bellows; even if he does not burn you with the sparks of his fire, his foul-smelling air will surely reach you.” This hadith has also been narrated by Ahmad bin Amr bin Abdul Khaliq al-Bazzar in “Musnad Abi Musa” through the chain of Khallad bin Aslam Marwazi from Nadr bin Shumail from ‘Awf from Qasamah bin Zuhair from Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The example of a good companion is like that of a perfume seller; he will either give you some perfume as a gift, or you will get fragrance from his clothes. And the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith; even if he does not burn your clothes, he will surely give you a foul smell, or his smoke will continue to trouble you.” Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Amr said: And this hadith has also been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) in a mawquf (stopped at the Companion) form, and we do not know of anyone besides Nadr bin Shumail who has narrated it as marfu‘. This (Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Amr) is Bazzar’s error, because Yahya bin Ma‘in has narrated it as marfu‘ through the chain of Sufyan bin ‘Uyaynah from Burayd bin Abi Burdah from Abi Burdah from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him). And Yahya bin Ma‘in is a greater scholar than Bazzar, while Sufyan bin ‘Uyaynah is an Imam in hadith."
"1378","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The example of a good companion is like that of a perfume seller, and the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith who blows the bellows. Even if he does not burn you, his sparks will keep reaching you."
"1379","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a good companion is like that of a perfume seller, and the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith who blows the bellows. Even if he does not burn you, his sparks will keep reaching you."" Imam Bukhari (may Allah have mercy on him) has also narrated this hadith from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) in a marfu' form."
"1380","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The example of a good companion and a bad companion is like that of the one who carries musk and the one who blows the bellows of a blacksmith. So the musk carrier will either give you (some musk) as a gift, or you will buy it from him, or you will get a pleasant fragrance from him. And the one who blows the bellows of a blacksmith will either burn your clothes, or you will get a foul smell from him."
"1381","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the example of the believer who recites the Qur’an is like that of a citron, whose fragrance is pleasant and whose taste is good. And the example of the believer who does not recite the Qur’an is like that of a date, whose taste is good but it has no fragrance. And the example of the sinner who recites the Qur’an is like that of basil, whose fragrance is pleasant but its taste is bitter. And the example of the sinner who does not recite the Qur’an is like that of colocynth, whose taste is bitter and it has no fragrance. And the example of a good companion is like that of a musk seller; even if you do not get anything from him, his fragrance will surely reach you. And the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith’s furnace; even if you are not affected by its heat, its smoke will surely reach you.”"
"1382","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of a good companion is like that of a perfume seller; even if you do not get any of his perfume, you will surely experience its fragrance. And the example of a bad companion is like that of a blacksmith; even if his sparks do not burn you, his smoke will surely trouble you."
"1383","Hasan says that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The example of the obligatory prayer is like a scale; whoever keeps it complete will receive complete reward."
"1384","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My example and the example of this world is just like that of a rider who rested for a while under the shade of a tree on a very hot day at noon, then left it and moved on."
"1385","The brother of Bani Qahr, Sayyiduna Mustawrid (may Allah be pleased with him), reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is like that of one of you dipping his forefinger into the sea, then (taking it out and) seeing how much water it returns with."
"1386","Sayyiduna Mustawrid Qahari (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is like that of one of you dipping his forefinger into the sea, then (taking it out and) seeing how much water it returns with."" Muslim ibn Hajjaj narrated it from a group (of hadith scholars), among whom is Muhammad ibn Hatim, and these are his words. He said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us with his chain in this manner and said: ""Like one of you dips this finger,"" and Yahya ibn Sa'id gestured with his forefinger."
"1387","Sayyiduna Mistawrid Fahri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world in comparison to the Hereafter is like one of you dipping his finger into the sea, then (taking it out and) seeing how much water it returns with."
"1388","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for a servant, He makes him honey."" The Companions asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by making him honey?"" He replied: ""He guides him to a righteous deed, then seizes his soul while he is upon it."
"1389","Sayyiduna Abu Anbasah Khawlani رضي الله عنه narrates from the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم that he صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Indeed, when Allah intends good for a servant, He makes him honey."" The companions asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by making him honey? He replied: ""He opens for him the door of righteous deeds. Then He seizes his soul while he is upon that (righteous deed)."
"1390","Sayyiduna Amr bin Humaq (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! How does He employ him? He said: ""He guides him to a righteous deed before his death."
"1391","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends to seize the soul of a servant in a certain piece of land, He creates a need for him there."
"1392","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Azza (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this statement... (The narrator of the hadith) Ayyub said: or he said (instead of ""there"") ""there is no need."
"1393","Abu Mulaikh narrates from a man of his people, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""When Allah wants to seize the soul of a servant in a piece of land, He creates a need for him there."
"1394","Abu Mulaikh narrates from his people, they said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""When Allah Almighty wants to seize someone's soul from somewhere, He creates a need for him there."
"1395","Sayyiduna Matar bin ‘Ukats (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When Allah Almighty wants to seize the soul of a servant in a piece of land, He creates some need for him there.”"
"1396","Sayyiduna Rafi‘ bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “When Allah loves someone, He protects him from the world just as one of you protects his sick one from water.”"
"1397","Sayyiduna Qatadah bin Nu’man (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"1398","Sayyiduna Atiyyah Sa'di (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a ruler becomes enraged, Satan takes control over him."
"1399","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a slave is sincere to his master and worships his Lord in a good manner, then for him there is a double reward."
"1400","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a slave is sincere to his master and worships his Lord in a good manner, then for him there is a double reward."
